{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread","id":1213444,"title":"Arcanist's Mage Homebrew Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-30T08:44:57-07:00","id":1213444,"title":"Arcanist's Mage Homebrew Thread","content":"So I have been doing a lot of thinking about Mage, how it functions, and ways that it could better evoke cultural and folkloric ideas of magic and those who practice it. There's also a couple of things about how certain subsystems, like Summoning Supernal Beings, Mage Sight, and making Imbued Items, function that just kind of rub me the wrong way. I kind of like how, for the most part, 2E has moved away from making the number of successes on a roll not dramatically affect most actions outside of Extended Actions or things like Chases or Combat. So I've been tweaking and poking at the rules to see how, if at all, they could be made a little more elegant.<br /> <br /> Summoning Supernal Beings is one of the things that kind of bugged me the most, if only because it didn't <i>feel </i>right. Ritual actions in Mage 2E, especially for Attainments, tend to be rather precise and calculated. Summonings of this style in folklore and various occult traditions in the real world are procedures undertaken with a lot of thought and a lot of research beforehand. They depend on preparation and correct action instead of mostly random chance. I've altered the rules ever so slightly (and tweaked Supernal Beings a little to match) to better fit that feeling. <hr /><br /> <b>Truth Manifest- Supernal Beings</b><br /> <br /> Normally, the Supernal World doesn\u2019t interfere with the Fallen one; it simply rests in the background, a Tapestry of symbols backlit by light casting shadows on the walls of Plato\u2019s cave. In this way, it acts a lot like a phase of Twilight, one that the Awakened gain unique insight to with their Sight. Normally, those symbols are inert, but Mages are creatures of symbolism and semiotics at heart, and they can wake them into action. Supernal Beings exist naturally in Aedes and Emanations, where the symbolism of the Supernal World is manifest, or as the Bound, fallen god-monsters imprisoned, trapped, or conscripted to guard Ruins of the Time Before, but can be summoned (some might argue <i>created</i>) by Disciples of the Arcana in accordance with the Gnosis of their Path.<ul><li><b>Attributes: </b>Supernal Beings follow the normal rules for Ephemeral Beings</li> <li><b>Manifest Truth:</b> Summoned Supernal Beings do not possess Manifestations, and are normally Materialized, but may spend a point of Mana to conceal themselves within the Supernal World (where they are visible to Focused Mage Sight alone) or use spells to attune themselves to phases of Twilight. They can simply cancel the spell or spend another point of Mana to Materialize again.</li> <li><b>Arcana:</b> Instead of Influences and Numina, Supernal Beings possess two Arcana with dots equal to Rank, behaving otherwise as Mages when it comes to free Spell Factors and Attainments, but rolling Power + Finesse for spellcasting, and using Rank instead of Gnosis for things like Combined Spells and Yantras. Supernal Beings have unlimited Paradox-free Reach to use on spells and can activate Reach abilities at will so long as the spell remains under their control, but must spend Mana to use spells accordingly if they use an Arcanum that is not one of the Ruling Arcana of the Path they represent, or spells that break the limits of the Lie.</li> <li><b>Boons:</b> Every Supernal Being possesses a Boon, a unique ability related to either their Primary or Secondary Arcanum. They gain an additional Boon per dot of Rank over three (IE. A Rank 5 Angel has three Boons) and can sacrifice dots of their Arcana for more.</li> <li><b>Thaumavore:</b> Supernal Beings can only normally replenish Mana using spells, but they can also devour the Mana in an object or being\u2019s Pattern, gaining Mana equal to the Size of an animal, all Mana stored in an object, or Health x3 in the case of a human (what a Mage would get Scouring them to death). Awakened are tempting targets for the Bound because they also gain any Mana in the Mage\u2019s Pattern as well as another point of Mana per dot of Gnosis. They spend a point of Mana per day to remain active in the Fallen World and regain Mana equal to their Rank per day in an Emanation or Aedes. They also bleed a point of Mana per scene outside an area Resonant with their symbolism.</li> <li><b>Other Traits:</b> Supernal Beings possess a Virtue and Vice, but they need not be anything a human would recognize as such and they are fundamentally coloured by the Realm the Supernal Being is attuned to. Additionally, the Supernal Being possesses a Ban and a Bane. Common Bans for Supernal Beings are Trials that render them metaphysically incapable of assisting those who haven\u2019t passed them, or obligating the Supernal Being to aid those who pass the Trial.</li> </ul><i>Modified Attainment- Targeted Summoning</i><br /> <br /> Supernal Beings are magic made manifest, and even the most pitiful of them knows more about magic than most Awakened could ever hope to learn. Summoning their aid, then, is something to be desired, but it is dangerous and risky, something reserved only for those who truly dedicate themselves to the Mysteries of their Path. The Summoning is an Attainment that can only use free Reach and without free Spell Factors. The Summoning takes a scene, and the Scale Factor helps determine the radius of the summoning circle, the \u201csafe zone\u201d for the Supernal Being, while Potency is used against the Withstand of the Supernal Being's Rank. It costs a point of Mana to use the Attainment, and an additional point of Mana to specify the second Arcanum of the Supernal Being (provided you have another Arcanum at three dots). Summoning Mages may use any suitable Yantras and can benefit from the aid of other Awakened, but suffer a penalty equal to the Gnosis of the highest-Gnosis Mage of another Path present or participating in the ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Note- Home Address:</b> A Mage summoning a Supernal Being known to dwell in a particular Aedes or Emanation gains a +4 Environmental Yantra bonus to the summoning if the Summoning is performed in the area of the Aedes or an Emanation's Iris. If they have completely understood the Aedes\u2019 Mystery, they gain an additional point of Reach for the summoning.<br /> <br /> <b>Note- Abyssal Intrusion:</b> In a contested roll against the Attainment is a base dice pool of the participants\u2019 Gnosis-derived Paradox pools, with additional dice based on the Abyssal taint and Paradox Conditions that all participating Mages are suffering from. Add a +1 if any Sleepers witness the Summoning, with the 9-again quality for a small group and the 8-again quality for a crowd. If the Paradox roll succeeds against the Summoning roll, then an Abyssal Being of equivalent Rank is summoned instead. Mana can be spent by participating Mages to reduce the Paradox pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Note- Fallen and Bound:</b> While Supernal Beings are powerful, they are vulnerable in the Fallen World. Within the summoning circle they are safe, but outside of the circle they suffer a point of Resistant Lethal Damage per scene, or reduce an Attribute by one as if it had been Scoured. The same thing occurs if a Mage suffers a Paradox in their vicinity one-to-one for Paradox successes, and the same for Dissonance caused by Sleepers. When the Duration of the Attainment runs out, if the Supernal Being isn\u2019t within the circle then they treat the entire Fallen World as a Bane until it escapes or dies. If the Supernal Being is killed outside of the summoning circle, or is destroyed by deliberate magical attack, then they fall to the Abyss, destroyed in an obvious fashion. When killed within the circle, it returns to the Supernal World or its home Emanation. If the Reach and Mana has been dedicated to make the Attainment Indefinite, then the Supernal Being becomes one of the Bound. If one of the Bound is killed within the confines of the Scale Factor of the summoning, it simply reforms in the area, waking when exposed to the presence of Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-30-2018, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T17:00:24-07:00","id":1213593,"title":"","content":"So a simplification of the summoning rules into a single spell-like roll, and making the Bound more numerous in-setting? Sounds workable, although the latter might have unforeseen setting implications. <br /> <br /> If summoning is akin to a spellcasting roll, what does Potency do? Used to overcome Withstand, which is equal to the entity\u2019s Rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T17:09:23-07:00","id":1213599,"title":"","content":"I'd argue making it a spell makes a Summoning far too easy.<br /> As written, you can only decrease the number of successes through Demesnes (and similar locations) as well as occult accoutrements.<br /> Which as a result, are really damn important as it's not easy for even a middling-tier Mage to summon anything more than a Rank 1-2 entity.<br /> <br /> When you're only rolling Gnosis + Arcanum, it's really easy to fail.<br /> <br /> If that's what you're going for, go ahead. But Summoning isn't easy, and if you want any chance, RAW, then you either need to abuse Fate, or use Occult tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:12:26-07:00","id":1213620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213593#post1213593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If summoning is akin to a spellcasting roll, what does Potency do? Used to overcome Withstand, which is equal to the entity\u2019s Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct, though I seem to have botched the writing on it. Obviously Scale and Duration are the two most important Spell Factors when using a summoning. I don't think it makes the Bound <i>exceptionally </i>more common, just gives them more places to come from apart from the Time Before. I like the idea of collapsing pocket dimensions, the crumbling Sancta of Masters, and the forgotten strongholds of the Orders being haunted by ornery, and more importantly, <i>hungry</i>, Supernal god-monsters. As it stands, the Attainment doesn't receive any free Spell Factors, and gets only three Reach maximum without Imperial magic, so making a Supernal Being one of the Bound still requires a -10 penalty to the roll, two Reach, and at least two Mana.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> As it stands, Summoning still isn't a spell, but rather a spell-like Attainment. A Demense is still a Yantra. Resonant tools are still Yantras. Ultimately, it's still the same, it just reduces the rolling to a minimum. Personally, without free Spell Factors I feel that it doesn't become any easier. Let's say that you have a bare minimum Mage looking to summon a Supernal Being. Without Yantras, you're rolling only four dice. If you're using the two best Yantras available, you've found an Aedes and an extremely rare otherworldly Sacrament to use as an offering (and bear in mind you can only use a given Sacrament <i>once </i>because it is used up in the roll), so now you're up to eleven dice. If you push yourself to the <i>absolute limit</i>, you have maybe five Spell Factors and a single Reach to use. To make the Summons even remotely useful, that Reach will have to be spent on Advanced Duration. If you don't extend Duration, or expand Scale, (and if you don't, then you've only got a Scene and the Supernal Being is standing in a circle that's only an arm's reach wide) then you, theoretically, could summon a Rank 5 Supernal Being.<br /> <br /> Again, you would need significant access to mystical resources to do so, at least a scene of prep, and only a scene of time with the Supernal Being. This also doesn't account for the Supernal Being's Ban, which is quite likely its Trial. If you go into it without prep, then you will, at best, have completely wasted your resources. At worst? You may have summoned an extraordinarily powerful Abyssal Being, and possibly destroyed a manifestation of the Supernal, which will be hell on your Wisdom and your reputation with the Awakened community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:35:50-07:00","id":1213623,"title":"","content":"Not exceptionally common, yes, but enough I think to make mages more wary of summonings in general. Except the Seers, who might attempt to Bind anti-Exarch entities of their own volition or under orders from Above. <br /> <br /> Mind if I use this idea of simplified summonings for my own stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:43:22-07:00","id":1213626,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts (if you are modifying Supernal Beings):<ul><li>This may affect longevity, but why treat Fallen Existence any different from Mana Bleed? Just require that Supernal Entities always have at least 1 Mana, and will Scour themselves Reflexively if and when necessary to keep it that way. Scouring will reduce Attributes and Corpus (with Resistant Lethal) anyways.</li> <li>How about treating the Summoning Circle as the appropriate Resonant Condition for the purposes of stopping Mana Bleed?</li> <li>Instead of dropping Numina entirely, what about allowing the Entity to replace them with Praxis, like Ghost Mages do?</li> </ul>Also: I too have issues with Imbued items - I just don't feel like the existing rules are quite <i>right</i>. Still uncertain exactly how, and what I'd change, but I'm working on a few ideas periodically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T19:40:48-07:00","id":1213637,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Not at all! Go right ahead. Honestly, I think that properly fits the ideas of what Summoning <i>is </i>and who's supposed to be allowed to do it. The majority of historical grimoire texts were in the possession of clergy and nobility. You need a place in the Great Chain of Being a few steps up from the common man. The Cunning Folk, the hedge witches, they were unworthy. The only ones to call down Angels and call up Demons were those in positions of power with ordination from Above.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> With regards to longevity and Mana Bleed, using just Mana Bleed would make them much more durable. Scouring is still an option, but it doesn't leave them as quickly diminished, especially if they're encountering primarily Mages and other supernatural beings. If they're dealing with mortals, well, they start dying a lot more quickly. Would you still keep the whole &quot;treating the Fallen World as a Bane when Duration runs out&quot; thing? <hr /><br /> Anywhere, here's my Imbued Item stuff. It's rough, thrown together in about half an hour, but for now, I like it.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued Item (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>An Imbued Item is an object enchanted by an Adept of Prime. The spell costs whatever Mana it normally would, and at least one Mana even if it normally would be costless, and calculates Reach as though the spell was cast at the minimum Arcana rating. The Imbued Item can store Mana equal to its dot rating, which it replenishes either through other spells, or at a rate of one point per scene when stored in the presence of a Hallow Resonant with the spell. Imbued Items roll their dot rating as the spellcasting dice pool. Awakened users can spend the item\u2019s Mana instead of their own to mitigate Paradox, but only up to the limit imposed by their Gnosis. Paradoxes from an Imbued Item cannot be contained, instead automatically releasing. If an Imbued Item includes an Arcanum Attainment, increase its dot rating by one. Imbued Items can include multiple spells so long as it doesn\u2019t exceed five dots. Mages may use suitable Yantras up to their Gnosis-derived limits.<br /> <br /> <b>Modified Attainment- Imbue Item</b><br /> The mage can infuse an item with magic, creating an Imbued Item. The mage can imbue an item with any spell she is capable of casting. Imbued items retain their magic indefinitely; a spell cast using an imbued item might run out, but the imbued item itself does not. Attainments may only be included if they modify a spell; for example, mages can imbue items with spells using Sympathetic Range, but may not imbue an item with Mage Armor or the ability to create Rotes. The spell imbued into an item remains in the item\u2019s creator\u2019s spell control, even if the item only casts that spell when activated. If an imbued item casts its spell multiple times, however, it still only takes up one spell control \u201cslot.\u201d Most mages relinquish spells after they have imbued them, but if the mage retains control over an item\u2019s spell, she may alter its spell factors when the item casts it, and even cancel it as though she cast it herself. By spending Mana equal to the item\u2019s rating, a mage can destroy an imbued item she retains spell control over, no matter where it is.<br /> <br /> <i>System</i><br /> <b>Cost: </b>Mana equal to the Imbued Item\u2019s dot rating <b>Dice Pool: </b>Gnosis + Prime - dot rating <b>Action: </b>Special; as Equipment Building<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The item is imbued with magical energy, but it is cursed. The object has a different effect, and a different trigger, than the caster was intending. Perhaps worst of all, the item also possesses the enchanter\u2019s Signature Nimbus.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>The Mage successfully imbues the item, but the magic is unstable. The item gains the Fragile or Volatile Condition.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The Mage imbues the item and it functions as intended. The enchanter decides if the item has a persistent spell on it, or if it is activated<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The item receives an unexpected benefit (such as the 9-again quality to the spellcasting roll, or the benefits of being a Praxis). Alternatively, the enchanting Mage may relinquish the Imbued Item from their spell control without a point or dot of Willpower.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It just occurs to me that I have no idea what relinquishing an Imbued Item unsafely even <i>does</i>. Would the Imbued Item's enchantment eventually unravel? What would extra Reach do for an Imbued Item that can be activated? Give the Wielder a pool of Reach to use? I would guess that with persistent spells it would only activate Reach options or impose Abyssal Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-30-2018, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T01:09:32-07:00","id":1213697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213637#post1213637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imbued Items roll their dot rating as the spellcasting dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this result in ridiculously small dicepools? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T01:45:45-07:00","id":1213702,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t have imbued items recover more than one point of mana per day in the presence of a resonant Hallow, and I\u2019d have that point count against that Hallow\u2019s mana per day limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:23:19-07:00","id":1213733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213697#post1213697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't this result in ridiculously small dicepools? </div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, that\u2019s also how the official rules for Imbued Items work... which is leaving many people puzzled. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll need to reread the corebook, but something inside me tells me that perhaps the intention was said dice pool (\u201cequal to Arcanum rating of imbued spell\u201d) being the <i>activation</i> pool, not the spellcasting pool from where you get spell factors from. If the book says otherwise, well, I\u2019m stumped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:56:04-07:00","id":1213764,"title":"","content":"I think imbued items should work similarly to the Hung spell; very rough idea here:<br /> <br /> I.e. re-usable use hung spell. Automatic activation (at the cost of mana). Spell effect is pre-cast; and you can activate it by spending Mana. You can only have one instance of the spell at the time.<br /> Having an imbued item on your person takes up spell tolerance. Creating the imbued item Requires casting the spell and spending WP dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:59:41-07:00","id":1213766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213637#post1213637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> With regards to longevity and Mana Bleed, using just Mana Bleed would make them much more durable. Scouring is still an option, but it doesn't leave them as quickly diminished, especially if they're encountering primarily Mages and other supernatural beings. If they're dealing with mortals, well, they start dying a lot more quickly. Would you still keep the whole &quot;treating the Fallen World as a Bane when Duration runs out&quot; thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bane deals Aggravated (dealing Mana loss as well?), right? Should work. EDIT: Or, after duration expires, they simply can't regain Mana (except through self-Scouring?).<br /> <br /> Idea was that, in the right circumstances, Supernal Entities might exist in the Fallen World fairly long (getting Mana from other sources, keeping away from Paradox, etc.) and to unify the rules so there isn't so much to keep track of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213637#post1213637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anywhere, here's my Imbued Item stuff. It's rough, thrown together in about half an hour, but for now, I like it.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued Item (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>An Imbued Item is an object enchanted by an Adept of Prime. The spell costs whatever Mana it normally would, and at least one Mana even if it normally would be costless, and calculates Reach as though the spell was cast at the minimum Arcana rating. The Imbued Item can store Mana equal to its dot rating, which it replenishes either through other spells, or at a rate of one point per scene when stored in the presence of a Hallow Resonant with the spell. Imbued Items roll their dot rating as the spellcasting dice pool. Awakened users can spend the item\u2019s Mana instead of their own to mitigate Paradox, but only up to the limit imposed by their Gnosis. Paradoxes from an Imbued Item cannot be contained, instead automatically releasing. If an Imbued Item includes an Arcanum Attainment, increase its dot rating by one. Imbued Items can include multiple spells so long as it doesn\u2019t exceed five dots. Mages may use suitable Yantras up to their Gnosis-derived limits.<br /> <br /> <b>Modified Attainment- Imbue Item</b><br /> The mage can infuse an item with magic, creating an Imbued Item. The mage can imbue an item with any spell she is capable of casting. Imbued items retain their magic indefinitely; a spell cast using an imbued item might run out, but the imbued item itself does not. Attainments may only be included if they modify a spell; for example, mages can imbue items with spells using Sympathetic Range, but may not imbue an item with Mage Armor or the ability to create Rotes. The spell imbued into an item remains in the item\u2019s creator\u2019s spell control, even if the item only casts that spell when activated. If an imbued item casts its spell multiple times, however, it still only takes up one spell control \u201cslot.\u201d Most mages relinquish spells after they have imbued them, but if the mage retains control over an item\u2019s spell, she may alter its spell factors when the item casts it, and even cancel it as though she cast it herself. By spending Mana equal to the item\u2019s rating, a mage can destroy an imbued item she retains spell control over, no matter where it is.<br /> <br /> <i>System</i><br /> <b>Cost: </b>Mana equal to the Imbued Item\u2019s dot rating <b>Dice Pool: </b>Gnosis + Prime - dot rating <b>Action: </b>Special; as Equipment Building<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The item is imbued with magical energy, but it is cursed. The object has a different effect, and a different trigger, than the caster was intending. Perhaps worst of all, the item also possesses the enchanter\u2019s Signature Nimbus.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>The Mage successfully imbues the item, but the magic is unstable. The item gains the Fragile or Volatile Condition.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The Mage imbues the item and it functions as intended. The enchanter decides if the item has a persistent spell on it, or if it is activated<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The item receives an unexpected benefit (such as the 9-again quality to the spellcasting roll, or the benefits of being a Praxis). Alternatively, the enchanting Mage may relinquish the Imbued Item from their spell control without a point or dot of Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the ideas I was working on for Imbued Items were:<ul><li>Why the heck is the Dice Pool so small for lower rated Arcana? Shouldn't those be easier to use?<ul><li>Normalize it to: User's Gnosis + Arcana or Willpower (- Arcana of the spell?), whichever is higher.</li> <li>Creator defined - Attribute (Gnosis or Arcana?) + Skill, as determined by the nature of the item. Like assigning a Muldra to a Rote.</li> <li>Fix it to that specific Imbued Item (see below)</li> </ul></li> <li>So, Imbued Item is basically having the Spell, but at the minimum required rating and ignores Spell Control? Everything else is just as open?<ul><li>Fix many of the Spell Factors when the Item is created - If you make a Wand of Fireballs (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Thunderbolt, reskinned to Fire instead of Lightning) to cast at Area Scale, it will only cast at the Area Scale set, same for Potency etc.</li> <li>Other factors like Reach, etc. are also set when first Imbued.</li> <li>Remaining Dice Pool (as if the spell would have been cast normally) is the Activation Dice Pool.</li> <li>Leave some Spell Factors adjustable, but it affects the Activation Dice Pool (in which case, fixing them should grant a discount in return for the reduced flexibility?)</li> <li>EDIT: Yantras <i>can</i> be included on the casting/activation pool but are also pre-defined ahead of time. And required? Such that Environmental Yantra using items can only be used in appropriate environments?</li> </ul></li> <li>Do something with Spell Control limits and Paradox?<ul><li>Maybe you can &quot;set&quot; the effective Gnosis of the Imbued Item (increasing dot rating and successes)? This would be its Spell Control. And other Gnosis-derived factors?</li> <li>Paradox is automatically either Released or Contained, but if Contained, starts degrading the Imbued Item and/or infecting its spells?</li> </ul></li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213637#post1213637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: It just occurs to me that I have no idea what relinquishing an Imbued Item unsafely even <i>does</i>. Would the Imbued Item's enchantment eventually unravel? What would extra Reach do for an Imbued Item that can be activated? Give the Wielder a pool of Reach to use? I would guess that with persistent spells it would only activate Reach options or impose Abyssal Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about any Paradox Reach incurred start affecting the item's spells? Exceptional Success eventually &quot;breaks&quot; the imbued item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-01-2018, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T08:14:52-07:00","id":1213798,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11997\" data-vbnamecard=\"11997\">MovingMind</a> that's actually RAW, believe it or not. I'm not sure I like it either, but I start as close to the written rules as possible and then try to nudge out into more &quot;fringe&quot; ideas.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> that's actually RAW as well, except it doesn't add the &quot;in the presence of a Resonant Hallow&quot; clause. It just says &quot;in the presence of Mana&quot;. So you could carry it on your person as a Mage or Proximus and the Imbued Item would naturally recharge by draining your stores. But I had the exact same idea as you; I was toying with having it replenish only one Mana per day. Honestly, I think I prefer that. Mages are all about preparation, right? And if they need to refuel more quickly, that's what Prime spells are for.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> RAW, Imbued Items wielded by the Awakened do include their Gnosis (and if I was ST I'd allow them to use Yantras up to their Gnosis-based limit). But I see your point for non-Mage users. Perhaps cribbing from the rules for Proximi spellcasting would work? (Minus Paradox completely cancelling the spell) I'm not sure I like pre-establishing Spell Factors when creating the Imbued Item, except for persistent effects, and I'm not sure with persistent Imbued Items you'd even need to care about Duration, just its effective Potency or Scale. I'm also not sure I like the idea of effective Gnosis for Imbued Items. Too much overlap with Artifacts.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, didn't you have an idea of Artifacts as pseudo-Legacies? I like that idea quite a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T08:42:39-07:00","id":1213803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213798#post1213798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> RAW, Imbued Items wielded by the Awakened do include their Gnosis (and if I was ST I'd allow them to use Yantras up to their Gnosis-based limit). But I see your point for non-Mage users. Perhaps cribbing from the rules for Proximi spellcasting would work? (Minus Paradox completely cancelling the spell) I'm not sure I like pre-establishing Spell Factors when creating the Imbued Item, except for persistent effects, and I'm not sure with persistent Imbued Items you'd even need to care about Duration, just its effective Potency or Scale. I'm also not sure I like the idea of effective Gnosis for Imbued Items. Too much overlap with Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what I was thinking of was more the Imbue process is basically allowing an Item to replicate a specific spell casting, over and over (powered by Mana). In that regard, the Spell Factors are already determined by the initial casting when it is then Imbued into the item. Flexibility after the fact, would be an extra/bonus (though I just reread the Imbue Item text, and maybe this is already RAW? It mentions a Mage that keeps the Imbued spell in Spell Control can adjust the Spell Factors as the item casts it - implying that Relinquished spells are entirely fixed?).<br /> <br /> Duration still matters for the Spell the Imbued Item casts (the Imbuement itself is Indefinite).<br /> <br /> As for Gnosis, as it stands, Imbued Items have no Spell Control limits. One item (properly supplied with Mana, and of sufficient Duration for the effect) can enchant an entire army in time.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Other Imbued Item ideas:<ul><li>Removing it from Prime 4 and making it a common Arcana 3 Attainment.</li> <li>Allowing non-spell Attainments to be Imbued. You want an Item that basically gives you Mage Armor, or temporary Spirit Rank? Go ahead. An Imbued item <i>could</i> even make Rotes, but only one so there really isn't any point.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213798#post1213798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, didn't you have an idea of Artifacts as pseudo-Legacies? I like that idea quite a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do. (And more Proximus Dynasties, and People-as-Imbued-and-Enhanced-Items-as-a-minor-template, and more Horrors, and a Condition-and-Nightmare-using-minor-template for Beast, and a Demon Fantasy Shard, and...)<br /> <br /> Basic Idea was to build the Artifact as if it were a custom Legacy - Oblations to recharge its Mana, Attainments that ignored Paradox (but the effects were fixed), etc. Might ignore the usual 1-to-5 Attainments restriction that legacies use. Thinking about it more, one could also treat them as a bonus &quot;2nd Legacy&quot;, with features that unlock based on the user's Gnosis and Arcana understandings.<br /> <br /> I really should finish some of my projects...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-01-2018, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T08:54:25-07:00","id":1213811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213803#post1213803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, what I was thinking of was more the Imbue process is basically allowing an Item to replicate a specific spell casting, over and over (powered by Mana). In that regard, the Spell Factors are already determined by the initial casting when it is then Imbued into the item. Flexibility after the fact, would be an extra/bonus (though I just reread the Imbue Item text, and maybe this is already RAW? It mentions a Mage that keeps the Imbued spell in Spell Control can adjust the Spell Factors as the item casts it - implying that Relinquished spells are entirely fixed?).<br /> <br /> Duration still matters for the Spell the Imbued Item casts (the Imbuement itself is Indefinite).<br /> <br /> As for Gnosis, as it stands, Imbued Items have no Spell Control limits. One item (properly supplied with Mana, and of sufficient Duration for the effect) can enchant an entire army in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I see your point. So how would you modify the Attainment then? Also, the way I read Imbued Item is that while it doesn't count against <i>your </i>Spell Control, as the Imbued Item doesn't have Gnosis it would incur an additional unsafe Reach per spell past the first. Eventually the Imbued Item would become horrifically unstable.<br /> <br /> With regards to Artifacts, that was my idea as well! The main bonus of Artifacts is that they have their own Gnosis and Arcana, and thus their own Spell Control. Awakened users can immediately gain access to Arcana they didn't have before. Sleepwalkers with the proper Merit can then effectively become pseudo-Awakened. I especially like the idea of them having their own Attainments and Oblations. Makes them much more valuable to the Awakened than just &quot;free Spell Control and Arcana&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T09:26:32-07:00","id":1213815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213811#post1213811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... I see your point. So how would you modify the Attainment then? Also, the way I read Imbued Item is that while it doesn't count against <i>your </i>Spell Control, as the Imbued Item doesn't have Gnosis it would incur an additional unsafe Reach per spell past the first. Eventually the Imbued Item would become horrifically unstable.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: the Awakening, pg. 196</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell imbued into an item remains in the item\u2019s creator\u2019s spell control, even if the item only casts that spell when activated. If an imbued item casts its spell multiple times, however, it still only takes up one spell control \u201cslot.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like free Spell Control to me, as opposed to incurring Exceeds-Spell-Control-Reach.<br /> <br /> Leave the &quot;Making this item an Imbued Item&quot; process as is (or not), and use one of the alternate Activation Pool methods above. Maybe treat Spell Control as another upgradeable feature, just like extra Mana capacity? Or maybe unify the Dot effect and let it store Mana equal to Dots, and have Spell control equal to half dots?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213811#post1213811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to Artifacts, that was my idea as well! The main bonus of Artifacts is that they have their own Gnosis and Arcana, and thus their own Spell Control. Awakened users can immediately gain access to Arcana they didn't have before. Sleepwalkers with the proper Merit can then effectively become pseudo-Awakened. I especially like the idea of them having their own Attainments and Oblations. Makes them much more valuable to the Awakened than just &quot;free Spell Control and Arcana&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Artifacts let Mages use their Arcana as normal (though I thought that too). Their Arcana rating is simply for calculating the Reach and potency of its own spell effects.<br /> <br /> Artifacts are: Fancy Magical Effects (of Arcana the Mage might not have), plentiful Mana stores, and a +1 Path Tool. Kinda unimpressive, if you ask me. Those can all be duplicated via other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-01-2018, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T07:22:08-07:00","id":1225567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1213444-arcanist-s-mage-homebrew-thread?p=1213815#post1213815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like free Spell Control to me, as opposed to incurring Exceeds-Spell-Control-Reach.<br /> <br /> Leave the &quot;Making this item an Imbued Item&quot; process as is (or not), and use one of the alternate Activation Pool methods above. Maybe treat Spell Control as another upgradeable feature, just like extra Mana capacity? Or maybe unify the Dot effect and let it store Mana equal to Dots, and have Spell control equal to half dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I took another stab at the whole &quot;reworking Imbued Items&quot; thing. Dice pools are still abysmal for the non-Awakened unless the Imbued Item has a persistent spell enchanted within it, but given the dangers of Dissonance and Quiessence, it's probably safer that way. <hr /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Modified Attainment- Imbue Item</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The mage can infuse an item with magic, creating an Imbued Item. The mage can imbue an item with any spell she is capable of casting. Imbued items retain their magic indefinitely; a spell cast using an imbued item might run out, but the imbued item itself does not. Attainments may only be included if they modify a spell; for example, mages can imbue items with spells using Sympathetic Range, but not Mage Armor or the ability to create Rotes. The spell imbued into an item remains in the item\u2019s creator\u2019s spell control, even if the item only casts that spell when activated and only takes up one spell control \u201cslot.\u201d Multiple spells may be imbued into one item using the rules for Combined Spells. If the mage retains control over an item\u2019s spell, she may alter its Spell Factors, and even cancel it. By spending Mana equal to the item\u2019s rating, a mage can destroy an imbued item she retains spell control over, no matter where it is. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Note- Unsafe Relinquishing: An Imbued Item relinquished unsafely does not have unsafe Reach allocated, and as such rolls a chance die. Each success adds a Reach to the Imbued Item\u2019s pool, meaning that such Imbued Items can become dangerously powerful before spontaneously losing all power with an Exceptional Success.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Cost: </b>Mana equal to the Imbued Item\u2019s dot rating <b>Dice Pool: </b>Gnosis + Prime - dot rating</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Action: </b>Special; as Equipment Building</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The item is imbued, but it is cursed. The object has a different effect, and a different trigger, than the caster was intending.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Failure: </b>The item\u2019s magic is unstable. The item gains the Fragile or Volatile Condition.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Success: </b>The Mage imbues the item and it functions as intended. The enchanter decides if the item has a persistent spell on it, or if it needs to be activated.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Exceptional Success: </b>The item receives an unexpected benefit (such as the 9-again quality to the spellcasting roll, or the benefits of being a Praxis). Alternatively, the enchanting Mage may relinquish the Imbued Item from their spell control without a point or dot of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued Item (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>An Imbued Item is an object enchanted by an Adept of Prime. The spell costs whatever Mana it normally would, and at least one Mana even if it normally would be costless, calculating Reach as though the spell was cast at the minimum Arcana rating. The item stores Mana equal to its dot rating, which it replenishes either through other spells, or at a rate of one point per day when stored in the presence of a Resonant Hallow. Imbued Items roll their dot rating as the spellcasting dice pool if they are activated and do not have spell control, meaning every spell cast after the first costs Reach. Awakened users add Gnosis and suitable Yantras to the roll. They can spend the item\u2019s Mana instead of their own to mitigate Paradox, but only up to their per turn limit. Paradoxes from an Imbued Item cannot be contained. Paradox dice accrue at a rate of one die per unsafe Reach for non-Awakened users. If an Imbued Item includes an Arcanum Attainment, increase its dot rating by one. If you want to have the spell cast at a higher Arcanum level than its base (allowing for more free Reach to be assigned and better free Spell Factor) add a dot. Imbued Items can include multiple spells using the rules for Combined Spells so long as the item\u2019s total dots spent on Arcana and Attainments doesn\u2019t exceed five. Researching an Imbued Item's triggers requires an Investigation with Clue elements equal to its dot rating.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> I also took a stab at the whole &quot;Artifacts as pseudo-Legacies&quot; thing. One of the things I like about this is that it makes Artifacts much more valuable to the Awakened than just &quot;fancy magical effects, Mana, and a +1 Yantra&quot;, especially because of the ways that Attainments differ from standard Supernal magic. Beyond that, this way the most powerful Artifacts can have up to ten different unique and strange abilities, and grant two Arcana up to the level of Mastery to their wielders. It also makes Sleepwalkers with the Relic Attuned Merit spectacularly dangerous pseudo-Awakened.<br /> <br /> <b>Artifact (\u2022\u2022 </b>to <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>Solidified Resonance and Mana transforms a symbol from the Supernal World into a physical object. Artifacts possess Gnosis equal to their dot rating, and two Ruling Arcana with dot ratings equal to half Gnosis, rounded up. They count as +2 Path Yantras for the Paths with their Arcana as Ruling Arcana or +3 if the Artifact\u2019s Gnosis is greater than the Mage who\u2019s wielding it. Artifacts can store Mana up to their Gnosis-based maximum, and have their own Oblations by which they may gather up to their Arcanum rating per day. Artifacts possess a number of Attainments (that follow the rules for Legacy Attainments, see <b>Mage: The Awakening pg. 198</b>) dependent on their Gnosis and Arcana ratings. If the Artifact contains only one, high-Gnosis, Attainment, reduce its dot rating by one. Mages may use their, or the Artifact\u2019s, Gnosis and Arcana in any combination, and may even wield the Artifact\u2019s traits for use in Creative Thaumaturgy. Each of the Artifact\u2019s Attainments possess unique triggers that can be researched using an Investigation requiring a number of Clue elements equal to twice its dot rating to discover without complication.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 06-07-2018, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T12:16:48-07:00","id":1242991,"title":"","content":"What about this for a hack for Unsafely Relinquishing Imbued Items:<br /> <br /> Their Mana supply becomes fixed, so once it runs out, the Imbuement ends. The Spell Factors and such are fixed, since it was Relinquished, and the periodic decay Unsafely Relinquished spells go through makes the whole thing unstable and gives it a shelf life. Works best for &quot;magic potions/scrolls&quot; and deliberately short-term items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}